  "body": "**Cause.** In `fanuc.cps`, `haas.cps`, `mazak.cps` and `sinumerik.cps`, the modal plane went back to G17 only in three places: before the next XY arc, before a canned cycle, and at section end. So a COMP engage (G41/G42 on the next G01) or a cancel (G40) that came after an XZ (G18) or YZ (G19) arc was written while G18/G19 was still the active plane, and the control compensated in that plane instead of XY. Nothing stopped an XZ/YZ arc from being written while comp was on either.\n\n**Fix (per script; plane and comp state live in the scripts, not the engine).** The same two helpers sit next to `restorePlane` in each of the four posts:\n- `compPlaneWord(cg)`: the block that writes G41/G42/G40 starts with `G17` when the modal plane is not 17, e.g. `G17 G01 G42 X0 Y0 Z-2 D02 F500`.\n- `compPlaneRefuse(g)`: an XZ/YZ arc that arrives while comp is engaged is refused by name with a counted warning, which blocks the post. It is not written, so the plane never switches under comp.\n\nFanuc, Haas, Mazak and Siemens 840D are all fixed. Heidenhain, Tormach and the Fanuc lathe already refuse control compensation. A program that never leaves G17 posts byte-identically, so no golden changed. This also makes the \"step back to G17 before comp\" workaround in PR #393's fixture unnecessary.\n\n**Readings.** All four posts now write G17 on the engage block after a G18 arc and after a G19 arc. The RS-274 modal check finds 0 faults. With the script changes stashed, the two pinning tests fail.\n\n**Pinning tests** (`crates/post/tests/comp_plane.rs`, a small RS-274 modal reader that checks the plane at every G41/G42/G40 and looks for a plane switch while comp is on):\n- `every_comp_post_states_g17_before_engaging_after_an_xz_or_yz_arc`\n- `every_comp_post_refuses_an_xz_or_yz_arc_while_compensation_is_engaged`\n- `a_program_that_never_left_g17_gets_no_extra_plane_word`\n\n**Gate.** camcraft-post: every test binary green (comp, comp_plane, post_engine, axis_direction_cli). camcraft-app: control_comp, wear_comp, conformance, golden_cl, fanuc_post, posting all green, goldens unchanged. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/391-comp-plane.md`.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc, Haas, Mazak and Siemens 840D posts state G17 on the cutter-compensation block after an XZ/YZ arc and refuse an XZ/YZ arc while compensation is engaged\n\nFixes #391\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
